cff-version: 1.2.0
title: EU AI Act für SaaS
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as part of the SimpleAct AI Governance Framework."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: SimpleAct-Compliance
repository-code: "https://github.com/SimpleAct-Compliance/simpleact-ai-act-for-saas"
license: MIT
abstract: "Where the provider/deployer line falls for software vendors under Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, and what breaks when the model underneath changes. Covers the role chain across model provider, vendor, customer and end user; the three records a vendor owes but cannot produce without the model provider; multi-tenancy including tenant-side configuration and per-tenant fine-tuning; the release gate as the single point where materiality under Art. 3(23), Art. 50 labelling and record validity are decided; and the four questions every enterprise procurement review asks."
keywords:
  - EU AI Act
  - SaaS
  - Article 25
  - Article 50
  - multi-tenancy
  - release management
  - model provider dependency
  - GPAI
  - AI governance
  - SimpleAct
